  "details": "<p>In 2008 the St. Stephanos monastery was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage site as part of the \"The Armenian Monastic Ensembles of Iran\". Located in the north-west of the country, this heritage listing consists of three monastic ensembles of the Armenian Christian faith: St Thaddeus and St Stepanos and the Chapel of Dzordzor.\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Armenian monastery in East Azarabaijan province, Iran. The first church was constructed on the site in 62 CE. A monastery was constructed there in the 7th century, and the structure was expanded in the 10th century.",
